Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.09,0:00:05.98,Main Top,Commander,0,0,0,,For these reasons, we have selected \Nthe five Eighty-Six, as well as the rest of Nordlicht,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.98,0:00:08.68,Main Top,Commander,0,0,0,,for the mission to destroy the Morpho.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.73,0:00:10.48,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,Detail Roster
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.48,0:00:15.81,Main Top,Commander,0,0,0,,This is my formal decision as\N Western Theater commander.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.82,0:00:14.82,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(482,473)}September 2nd, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.36,0:00:19.73,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,Even you don't have the right \Nto overrule—
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.73,0:00:22.78,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I know that. \NI was ready for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.48,0:00:25.51,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But I want to know one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.76,0:00:31.88,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,General, this isn't a year-late attempt \Nat a "disinfection," is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.25,0:00:36.67,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,There's no way that those children, \Nespecially just the five of them,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.67,0:00:39.84,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,can break through Legion-controlled territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.22,0:00:45.86,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Some of the officers had said \Nright when we took them in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.40,0:00:51.74,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,that it was better to eliminate them \Nfor the safety of the Federacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.12,0:00:54.49,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You were one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.92,0:01:00.12,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I won't deny your wish \Nto protect what you care for.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.53,0:01:04.55,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,However, this nation is built on justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.55,0:01:12.30,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,It's not acceptable for a human to try to have his way \Nusing violence, rather than using words.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.68,0:01:14.99,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,So I'm asking you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.46,0:01:18.67,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You can assure me this isn't \Nwhat it looks like, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.82,0:01:22.08,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.74,0:01:23.83,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.83,0:01:25.44,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,I want to hear your thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.80,0:01:26.93,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,On what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.35,0:01:30.09,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,They're not poor, pitiful children.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.09,0:01:32.87,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,They're monsters, created by the\N madness of the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.87,0:01:36.47,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,Are you willing to take them\N into your beloved homeland?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.47,0:01:39.95,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,Is that really what the Federacy should be?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.95,0:01:41.84,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.84,0:01:46.22,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Those are my ideals \Nand the ideals of the nation I lead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.59,0:01:50.96,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I speak on behalf \Nof the entire Federacy, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.30,0:01:56.21,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I am responsible for executing\N my duties with pride and dignity!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.82,0:02:00.31,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.41,0:03:41.35,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Oh, no, it's pitch black.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.75,0:03:43.87,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,You'll damage your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.87,0:03:46.63,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,I'm not willing to listen \Nto alternative plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.63,0:03:49.45,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I know. \NSo I have a suggestion.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.70,0:03:54.00,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,The reason you kept Nordlicht \Nsplit up into smaller platoons
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.00,0:04:02.17,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,was to keep the rest of the military \Nfrom realizing their strength, wasn't it, Richard?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.30,0:04:08.80,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,The Republic weapons we captured—\NJuggernauts, were they?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.80,0:04:13.43,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Once you've seen the combat logs on them, \Nit makes you want to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.24,0:04:19.25,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,A blade that cuts too well will either be avoided, or used until it breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.80,0:04:22.71,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Either way, it won't end well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.71,0:04:26.52,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,In the end, your fears came true, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.31,0:04:30.13,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Don't get too attached.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.13,0:04:36.06,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Even if we ever-so-kindly took them in, \Nthey would never forget the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.06,0:04:36.95,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I don't know about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.74,0:04:42.47,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,They're still kids in their mid-teens.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.47,0:04:44.97,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Right now, they're not used \Nto their new environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.97,0:04:46.99,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's all they can do \Nto protect themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.78,0:04:48.58,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.89,0:04:51.04,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Someday they might get used \Nto this country
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.04,0:04:55.23,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,and long to have the things \Nthat were stolen from them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.60,0:05:00.03,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,And even if they were still to choose \Nto live on the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.48,0:05:02.21,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,it should be their decision to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.48,0:05:04.61,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I'll wait until then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.20,0:05:06.81,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,However many years it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.10,0:05:10.15,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Do you have a duty to go that far?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.46,0:05:11.67,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.67,0:05:15.79,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's our responsibility for arrogantly \Ntrying to save our fellow humans
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.79,0:05:18.80,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,as you would a drowning puppy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.55,0:05:22.59,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,And you think a bloody blade, \Nforged and honed on the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.59,0:05:24.66,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,can understand human feelings?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.66,0:05:28.46,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,We made the same bet before. \NDo you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.46,0:05:30.63,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I won then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.63,0:05:34.59,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,And the Legion took all your winnings.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.97,0:05:35.84,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.71,0:05:47.61,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,Grethe, you simply see \Nthe dead in them. That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.43,0:05:51.53,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,You see what you can never get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.53,0:05:53.45,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,So what if I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.45,0:05:57.28,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,If you're that worried, \Nthen that'll make this easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.00,0:06:03.68,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Those slow transport helicopters aren't appropriate \Nfor my Reginleifs' big mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.29,0:06:06.42,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Give me permission to use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.43,0:06:13.43,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,September 13th, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.02,0:06:12.24,Main Top,Richard,0,0,0,,"It," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.71,0:06:20.17,Main,Old man staff,0,0,0,,I never thought I'd see the day \Nthe sealed door opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.17,0:06:22.39,Main,Woman staff,0,0,0,,Sometimes living a long time \Nhas its benefits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.59,0:06:24.07,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,"The sealed door"?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.07,0:06:26.36,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,That's what some call it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.65,0:06:30.33,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,If it's sealed, \Nthen it should be left that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.33,0:06:32.14,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Now, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.56,0:06:38.75,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.75,0:06:41.38,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,An old Imperial Air Force hangar.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.38,0:06:42.83,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,For a prototype.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.15,0:06:45.96,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,A prototype plane?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.20,0:06:47.11,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.11,0:06:50.61,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It completed its test flights \Nand was about to enter mass production
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.61,0:06:54.22,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,when the war started, and the\N base was temporarily abandoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.22,0:06:57.19,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,This place is right next \Nto the border.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.19,0:06:59.98,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I guess the Legion took it over real quick, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.41,0:07:11.87,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Why is it underground?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.26,0:07:15.84,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,A bunch of reasons. \NIt's safer from bombing this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.23,0:07:20.24,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It also means the Legion didn't take it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.57,0:07:28.95,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,This is the X-C1 "Nachzehrer," \Na prototype ground-effect vehicle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.73,0:07:32.43,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's still sleeping right now, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.49,0:07:35.73,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,It flies?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.73,0:07:37.34,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,"Ground-effect vehicle"?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.75,0:07:40.08,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,A plane that uses ground effect—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.08,0:07:43.14,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,which occurs when you stay right \Nabove the ground—to fly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.45,0:07:48.60,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It can get you to the Morpho far faster \Nthan a transport helicopter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.84,0:07:52.44,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Um, I think I heard you say, \N"right above the ground."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.67,0:07:53.52,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.52,0:07:56.95,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It flies only a few meters\N above the ground!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.23,0:08:02.71,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It flies lower than a cruise missile, \Nmaking it hard for radar and AA missiles to locate!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.19,0:08:05.11,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,That's the power of the Nachzehrer!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.92,0:08:08.06,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,What an awful name.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.52,0:08:11.38,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,A Nachzehrer is an old vampire legend \Nfrom the southeast part of the Federacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.73,0:08:15.63,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,It rises from its grave \Nand wanders the graveyard
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.63,0:08:20.80,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,while dragging its shadow behind it, \Nand rings the church bell.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.80,0:08:23.29,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Yeah, that is a nasty name.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.29,0:08:27.02,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Wait! We'll run into buildings\N if we're just a few meters off the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.23,0:08:30.27,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,This mission takes place \Nin former Imperial territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.27,0:08:32.21,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,We have the geographic data.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.21,0:08:35.38,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,The Legion doesn't make towns or homes. \NWe'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.66,0:08:37.36,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,What about the Legion themselves?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.66,0:08:39.39,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,We avoid them, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.39,0:08:41.20,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Nouzen can do that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.51,0:08:43.49,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I can tell you where they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.49,0:08:44.96,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But will it really work?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.46,0:08:50.19,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,This thing can't exactly turn on a dime, \Nso we'll have problems if we get ambushed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.19,0:08:55.48,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,But the three-country alliance will be handling \Nmost of the enemies, so we don't need to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.76,0:08:57.35,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,And then what?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.21,0:09:02.81,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,If we do get to the Morpho, \Ncan we win?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.81,0:09:06.44,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,And even if we do win, \Nwe'll be in the middle of enemy territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.44,0:09:08.28,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,How will we get back?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.27,0:09:14.79,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Well—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.79,0:09:18.61,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,It's more important to take out the Morpho \Nthan worry about how we'll get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.86,0:09:20.14,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.14,0:09:21.97,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Are you going to ignore it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.85,0:09:26.74,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You don't need me to tell you \Nwhat the result of that will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.81,0:09:30.11,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That said,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.11,0:09:32.88,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,you seem to take it for granted \Nthat this thing flies, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.23,0:09:35.10,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Who's going to pilot it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.69,0:09:38.10,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Who else?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.45,0:09:44.59,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.02,0:09:48.23,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.57,0:09:49.92,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,This isn't the time for jokes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.92,0:09:51.62,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Who's really going to do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.62,0:09:52.86,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Me, as I said!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.31,0:09:55.62,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's really me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.62,0:09:56.77,Main,Officers,0,0,0,,You're joking.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.77,0:09:57.98,Main,Officers,0,0,0,,That's ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.98,0:09:59.86,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's really me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.66,0:10:08.67,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(736,688)}October 7th, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.42,0:10:07.62,Main Top,Frederica,0,0,0,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.88,0:10:10.81,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Frederica.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.81,0:10:11.75,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm not leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.20,0:10:16.24,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I came because I heard you were \Nthrowing a tantrum about not leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.24,0:10:17.64,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,It's not a tantrum.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.64,0:10:20.45,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm a member of Nordlicht, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.45,0:10:23.27,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why do I have to be \Nthe only one to leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.27,0:10:25.77,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,It wouldn't be allowed anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.77,0:10:29.48,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You haven't forgotten what I said \Nabout mascots being hostages, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.48,0:10:32.74,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,An exception would be made \Nfor the president's daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.41,0:10:35.68,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.68,0:10:37.90,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why are you suddenly saying this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.15,0:10:42.84,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You're the one who said that nobody else \Nhas the right to decide how you live!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.84,0:10:47.92,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I also said it's best not to get involved \Nin someone's death if you don't have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.80,0:10:51.87,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.51,0:10:57.70,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I remember its voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.70,0:11:00.11,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I don't need you to show me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.40,0:11:01.99,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,It should be the other way around!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.99,0:11:03.97,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm the one with the relationship to Kiriya!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.30,0:11:06.22,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You should be the ones to go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.62,0:11:09.02,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'll talk to Grethe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.02,0:11:13.35,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You managed to survive the awful battles \Nin the 86th district.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.73,0:11:16.23,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You can't die in a plan like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.77,0:11:18.32,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'll handle this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.74,0:11:22.46,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You can see your knight,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.46,0:11:24.26,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,but not the other Legion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.26,0:11:26.78,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,If you head in, \Nyou and everyone else will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.78,0:11:27.59,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,But—!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.59,0:11:32.11,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Why are you so insistent on sending us \Nback to the rear?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.44,0:11:36.27,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Didn't you want us to kill your knight?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.10,0:11:40.26,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Or maybe you don't really\N want them dead at all?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.70,0:11:50.39,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Then head home. And forget it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.94,0:11:53.21,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You don't want to end up like me, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.73,0:11:56.67,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,And what about you? \NWhom do you think you're talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.35,0:12:05.21,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You followed your own brother onto \Nthe battlefield and slew his ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.21,0:12:09.25,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why are you telling me now that \NI can't chase my own ghost?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.56,0:12:12.59,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why are you telling me \NI can't achieve my goal?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.90,0:12:15.40,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You realize on some level, \Ndon't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.40,0:12:17.87,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,That having no goal, \Nno place to call "home,"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.87,0:12:20.00,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,clinging only to pride to keep you alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.00,0:12:22.78,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,is what made that pathetic ghost what he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.78,0:12:25.37,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Do you want to end up the same way?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.64,0:12:29.69,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I'm not your knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.82,0:12:32.59,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,You're free to see me in him if you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.95,0:12:38.00,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,But I don't want to be forced \Nto join in your regret and atonement.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.00,0:12:40.32,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You don't understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.32,0:12:42.62,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm telling you not to go!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.62,0:12:45.55,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why don't you obey, \Nyou impudent fool?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.55,0:12:49.79,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You regret not telling your brother \Nnot to go, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.79,0:12:54.24,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You still regret that he went to his death \Nwithout you saying anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.24,0:12:58.78,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,So why are you trying \Nto do the same thing he did?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.05,0:13:01.43,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why are you trying to make me suffer,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.43,0:13:04.62,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,as your brother made you suffer?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.85,0:13:13.02,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Frederica...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.15,0:13:17.36,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Don't go, Shinei...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.06,0:13:22.35,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I don't want you to die like Kiri.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.02,0:13:29.95,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I don't want... I don't want \Nany more people to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.58,0:13:36.95,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I don't want to lose another big brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.02,0:13:58.02,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(736,688)}October 9th, Stellar Year 2149
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.36,0:14:05.62,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,I'm amazed Frederica agreed not to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.94,0:14:09.36,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I don't think she agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.86,0:14:13.68,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,She's locked up in her room \Nand not even coming to see us off.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.68,0:14:15.80,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,She's the only one getting left behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.80,0:14:17.27,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That's enough reason to be grumpy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.27,0:14:21.01,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,If she's not going to the rear, \Nit doesn't matter what she is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.53,0:14:24.50,Main,Mechanic,0,0,0,,Everybody,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.01,0:14:27.75,Main,Mechanic,0,0,0,,get on board!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.38,0:14:31.00,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.00,0:14:31.59,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.59,0:14:32.84,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.84,0:14:34.19,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,You're sleepy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.19,0:14:36.83,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Normally I'd be asleep at this hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.83,0:14:38.23,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Sleep on the plane?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.23,0:14:39.92,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,I can't sleep on planes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.92,0:14:40.77,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.72,0:14:45.27,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.27,0:14:47.71,Main,Mechanic,0,0,0,,I hope it doesn't need to get used.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.70,0:14:52.28,Main Top,Grethe,0,0,0,,Everybody strapped in?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.28,0:14:56.75,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,30 minutes to mission start
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.50,0:14:53.95,Main Top,All,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.43,0:14:57.79,Italics Top,Shin,0,0,0,,You were telling the truth \Nabout being the pilot, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.79,0:14:59.28,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,We don't have another choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.28,0:15:02.63,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Most of the old Air Force's pilots \Ndied in combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.63,0:15:07.43,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I'm the only one who ever flew it \Nduring the test flights.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.43,0:15:10.92,Italics,Shin,0,0,0,,You mentioned being \Na former Air Force pilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.92,0:15:14.63,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,You sound as though \Nyou totally forgot until now, Lieutenant.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.06,0:15:18.68,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,I'm sure you forgot this, too, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.51,0:15:25.62,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,I'm opposed to kids like you \Ngoing out to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.23,0:15:32.20,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,To you Eighty-Six, fighting to the end here \Nis your source of pride, your identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.20,0:15:34.28,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,But I'm not giving up on this, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.86,0:15:36.80,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,If you're going to fight to the end,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.80,0:15:40.56,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,then my job is to fight
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.56,0:15:42.39,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,alongside you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.17,0:15:49.66,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,The country you finally reached \Nis far from a utopia.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.99,0:15:52.49,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,But remember this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.97,0:15:56.93,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,Not one person in this country \Nwants you to die in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.35,0:15:59.93,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,We want you to stay alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.70,0:16:04.35,Italics,Grethe,0,0,0,,That goes for me, the Division Commander, \Nand the rest of the unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.68,0:16:08.33,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,And me, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.16,0:16:11.44,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Hey, it's been a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.44,0:16:13.06,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,How are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.41,0:16:15.82,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.82,0:16:18.61,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm here to cheer you on, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.61,0:16:22.22,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm the highest ranking officer \Nin the Federacy Army, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.51,0:16:27.10,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,The Federacy's people, its territory, \Nand its neighbors are all in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.10,0:16:28.66,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I have to do at least this much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.37,0:16:32.64,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Especially since you're the core \Nof this mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.37,0:16:35.30,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.82,0:16:38.73,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Nordlicht's success in this mission will determine \Nthe fate of the Federacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.73,0:16:42.65,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,the surrounding countries, and humanity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.98,0:16:47.36,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Keep that in mind. \NAnd make sure you destroy the Morpho.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.85,0:16:50.37,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,We know you can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.93,0:16:52.85,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.48,0:16:55.16,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,And one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.01,0:16:58.22,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,This is your highest-priority mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.30,0:17:04.49,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Come back alive. \NAll of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.72,0:17:08.68,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,We'll do our best, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.68,0:17:09.95,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.95,0:17:11.72,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,We can't promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.93,0:17:13.62,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,That's not good enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.62,0:17:15.67,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,You need to come back, \Nno matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.06,0:17:17.68,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,You're fighting to the end, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.09,0:17:21.43,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,So you need to survive \Ntill the end of the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.96,0:17:26.91,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,So... come back. \NNo matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.98,0:17:37.03,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.77,0:17:39.77,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Come back, no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.99,0:17:43.52,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Or I'll...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.03,0:17:49.81,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,destroy this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.35,0:18:03.10,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,5 minutes to mission start
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.02,0:18:03.09,Main Top,Officer,0,0,0,,Mr. President.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.42,0:18:04.30,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.83,0:18:07.10,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.37,0:18:10.83,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Attention, comrades!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.90,0:18:17.85,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,The Western Theater forces will begin \Nan all-out march into Legion-held territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.49,0:18:21.75,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,This battle will determine not only the fate \Nof the Federal Republic of Giad,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.75,0:18:27.25,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,but also those of the United Kingdom of \NRoa Gracia, the Alliance of Wald,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.74,0:18:31.57,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,and the other nations whose cries for help\N we haven't even heard yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.57,0:18:37.83,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,This is the greatest operation \Nin the history of mankind!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.32,0:18:43.19,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You are the mighty shield \Nthat defends your homeland,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.19,0:18:47.03,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,and the sharp sword \Nthat cuts open a future for humanity!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.78,0:18:50.52,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We will be a symbol of justice \Nfor the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.84,0:18:53.77,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Keep our successful battles\N close to your heart
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.02,0:18:57.24,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,and advance, bravely, valiantly!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.01,0:19:22.70,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Begin the mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.70,0:19:23.80,Main,Female Soldier,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.80,0:19:24.61,Main,Soldier 1,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.61,0:19:25.39,Main,Soldier 2,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.10,0:19:49.19,Main,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Let's go, men!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.19,0:19:51.33,Main,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Advance!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.20,0:20:07.54,Main,Operator 1,0,0,0,,Flywheels 1 and 2 active.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.54,0:20:09.84,Main,Operator 1,0,0,0,,Temporary transformer operating normally.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.84,0:20:12.38,Main,Operator 2,0,0,0,,Initiating cooling of catapult rails.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.38,0:20:16.60,Main,Operator 2,0,0,0,,Coolant units operating at 23% and rising.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.52,0:20:21.13,Main,Operator 3,0,0,0,,Opening canopy. Deploying catapult rails.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.40,0:20:28.20,Main,Operator 1,0,0,0,,All joint locks deployed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.96,0:20:31.98,Main,Operator 1,0,0,0,,Nachzehrer, ready for takeoff!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.22,0:20:49.40,Main,Foxhole Soldier 1,0,0,0,,I've been waiting for this, \Nyou pieces of scrap.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.98,0:20:52.85,Main,Commander,0,0,0,,They're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.05,0:20:57.33,Main,Operator 4,0,0,0,,Phase 1 complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.66,0:21:00.45,Main,Operator 4,0,0,0,,We've succeeded in luring \Nthe Legion vanguard out of position.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.84,0:21:03.52,Main,Operator 4,0,0,0,,We will now move to phase 2.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.01,0:21:06.56,Italics,Operator 4,0,0,0,,Tiwaz HQ to Léraðr HQ.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.56,0:21:08.91,Italics,Operator 4,0,0,0,,Nachzehrer, you are cleared for take off!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.91,0:21:09.77,Main,Operator 1,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.77,0:21:12.28,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Okay, here we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.36,0:21:19.10,Italics,Operator 1,0,0,0,,Nachzehrer, take off!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.77,0:21:37.99,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Th-This is scarier than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.17,0:21:42.31,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Is the person who came up with this crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.65,0:21:47.47,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Oh, it's an honor to have you say that! \NI thought nothing scared you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.83,0:21:50.27,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,It's a little over 1000 km to our goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.27,0:21:53.19,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Enjoy our nine minutes or so\N in the sky!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.70,0:21:55.96,Main,Operator 4,0,0,0,,Nachzehrer has taken off successfully
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.27,0:21:58.94,Main,Operator 4,0,0,0,,and is proceeding as planned!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.26,0:22:14.30,Italics,Soldier 3,0,0,0,,Unit 4, signal lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.30,0:22:16.45,Italics,Soldier 4,0,0,0,,We've lost contact with the 2nd Company!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.45,0:22:19.91,Italics,Soldier 3,0,0,0,,Stay calm! Unit 1, Unit 2, keep going forward!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.91,0:22:22.13,Italics,Soldier 3,0,0,0,,Infantry, after us!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.82,0:22:24.02,Italics,Soldier 4,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.02,0:22:25.73,Italics,Soldier,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.31,0:22:33.86,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Give me a damage report! The battle's not over!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.62,0:22:37.52,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,If you have something \Nyou want to protect, then fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.52,0:22:40.11,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Raise your heads and go forward!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.57,0:22:44.12,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,The Federacy isn't retreating.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.60,0:22:45.95,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Just a little more!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.95,0:22:47.95,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Just hang in there a little more!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.95,0:22:51.91,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,And then those goddamn disgusting Eighty-Six will...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.91,0:22:54.98,Italics,Tank Soldier,0,0,0,,Then we'll win!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.33,0:22:57.64,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.64,0:23:01.41,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,If we take out the Morpho, we win, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.41,0:23:04.06,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We have to live up to their expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.06,0:23:06.91,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Yeah, if they're working that hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.91,0:23:08.68,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.93,0:23:39.93,sign_33925_337__If_There_s_Some,Anju,0,0,0,,"If There's Something Worth Dying For."
